[h1]VRV - Vacuum Recycler Variant[/h1]

[b]Overhauled mission DLLs for VSR[/b]

This build rewrites the entire salvage loop of the original campaign. Every
extractor, every scavenger route and every combat order was re-authored against
the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1325933293]VSR[/url]
mission table, so the recycling economy finally matches the unit list.

[img]https://i.ibb.co/PZWPsqnQ/ql50flhx.png[/img]
[img]https://i.ibb.co/spC8pKWd/0ypbm015.gif[/img]

[h2]Controls and Tactical Orders[/h2]

The command slot system is unchanged in spirit: you pick a slot, you give it a
role, and the craft decides how to satisfy it. What changed is that the roles
now survive a reload and a recycler rebuild.

[h3]Essential Hotkeys[/h3]

[table]
[tr][th]Hotkey / Command[/th][th]Unit / Target[/th][th]Tactical Behavior[/th][/tr]
[tr][td][b]7[/b][/td][td]Combat craft / Artillery[/td][td][b]Defend[/b]: Guards protect extractors and will not chase beyond the pool radius.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Ctrl+Space[/b][/td][td]Any unit[/td][td][b]Forced Go To[/b]: Ignores hostile fire and completes the move order even under attack.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Alt+7[/b][/td][td]Scavenger[/td][td][b]Scavenge[/b]: Claims the nearest scrap pool and returns with a full load.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Shift+1[/b][/td][td]Service Truck[/td][td][b]Repair[/b]: Repairs allied units inside its aura without being told twice.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]8[/b][/td][td]Recycler[/td][td][b]Recycle[/b]: Consumes the queued scrap pool and pauses the route while it works.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Ctrl+1[/b][/td][td]Extractor[/td][td][b]Hold[/b]: Stops the extraction cycle and keeps the deposit untouched.[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h3]Command Slot 6 (Autonomous Roles)[/h3]

[list]
[*][b]Combat Craft[/b]: Autonomous patrol between the extractor and the pool.
[*][b]Scavenger[/b]: Finds scrap pools inside the assigned sector only.
[*][b]Service Truck[/b]: Repairs allied units in the field, one target at a time.
[*][b]Recycler[/b]: Consumes queued scrap and reports when the queue is empty.
[*][b]Extractor[/b]: Holds the deposit and reports depletion in advance.
[/list]

[h3]Order Precedence[/h3]

[list=1]
[*]An explicit order from the player always wins over an autonomous role.
[*]A forced move ignores hostile fire but still respects the map boundary.
[*]A defensive order never leaves the extractor's guard radius.
[*]A scavenger route is abandoned when the pool is claimed by someone else.
[/list]

[h2]Economy Notes[/h2]

The recycled output is capped at the [i]deposit value[/i], not at the pool
total. That single change removes the old infinite-scrap exploit and makes the
recycler a logistics unit instead of a printing press.

[quote]If a recycler sits idle for more than one cycle, the queue is drained and the
scrap is returned to the pool with a small loss. Idle recyclers are expensive.[/quote]

[b]Thresholds[/b] are expressed on the craft's own hull, except where noted:

[list]
[*]Retreat to the recycler at [b](<25%, default)[/b] hull integrity.
[*]Abandon the pool at [b](<8%)[/b] remaining deposit value.
[*]Escort the scavenger when [b](2+ units)[/b] are reported in the sector.
[*]Repair priority follows the lowest hull value first.
[/list]

